<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-title>College Colors Day is October 1!
    </mj-title>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-text font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15px" color="#004C46" line-height="20px" />
      <mj-all font-family="Arial" />
      <mj-section padding="30px 0 0 0" />
      <mj-button background-color="#004C46" color="#FFF" border="2px solid #FFF" font-size="16px" border-radius="15px" font-weight="bold" letter-spacing="1px" />
      <mj-divider border-width="1px" />

    </mj-attributes>
    <mj-style inline="inline"> h2 { line-height: 28px; } a { color: #864e27; } a.dark { color: #004C46; } li { padding-bottom: 10px; } .dark-wrap { background: #004C46; color: #fff; } .light-wrap { background: #FFFFFF; } @media only screen and (max-width: 420px) { .caption div { text-align: center !important; } } </mj-style>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body background-color="#E9E3D0">
    <mj-section padding="40px 0 0">
      <mj-column>
        <!-- wordmark on right -->
        <!-- <mj-image src="https://mailings.humboldt.edu/polytechnic/img/header-right.png" alt="Cal Poly Humboldt" padding="0" /> -->
        <!-- wordmark on left -->
        <mj-image src="https://mailings.humboldt.edu/polytechnic/img/emailHeader-09262022.png" alt="Cal Poly Humboldt" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section css-class="light-wrap">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding-top="0">
          <h1 style="color:#004C45;font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;margin:0;text-align: left;"> A Message from Cal Poly Humboldt</h1>
          <p id="date" style="color:#004C45;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;margin:10px 0 20px 0;text-align: left;">September 10, 2026</p>
          <p style="color:#004C45;font-size:22px;font-weight:bold;margin:10px 0 20px 0; line-height:28px">College Colors Day is October 1!</p>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-divider border-color="#F2A900" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section css-class="light-wrap" padding-bottom="20px" padding-top="20px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="https://mailings.humboldt.edu/general/2026_09_10/spirit-grid.jpg"
                  alt="College Colors Day celebration featuring students in Cal Poly Humboldt green and gold colors, with kickball tournament action, face painting activities, and campus festivities"/>
        <mj-text>Mark your calendars and get ready to show your school spirit at <strong>College Colors Day, Thursday,
          Oct. 1</strong>.</mj-text>
        <mj-text padding-bottom="0">Join students, staff, faculty, and alumni for a campus-wide celebration filled with:</mj-text>
        <mj-text padding-top="0">
          <ul>
            <li>Free food and music—<strong>lunch served from noon–2 p.m.</strong></li>
            <li>Face painting, fun field games, and drawings for prizes</li>
            <li>The <strong>4th Annual Kickball Tournament Championship Game at 11 a.m. (</strong>Will anyone finally dethrone reigning champs 2 Legit 2 Kick?)</li>
          </ul>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>Bring your energy, your team colors, and your competitive spirit. Whether you’re battling for the trophy, painting your face, or just enjoying the music and atmosphere, it’s going to be an afternoon to remember. And it’s <strong>all FREE</strong>!</mj-text>
        <mj-text><strong>Thursday, Oct. 1 | 11 a.m. – 2 p.m. | Upper Playing Field near Redwood Bowl</strong></mj-text>
        <mj-text><strong>Don’t miss it!</strong></mj-text>

      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section padding="0 0 40px 0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="https://mailings.humboldt.edu/polytechnic/img/emailFooterDiamondH.png" alt="circle H graphic element" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>